 ## Relay and account data
 
 This section covers what the relay (`ferryx-relay`) and the account service it hosts keep on the operator's server, for example `relay.ferryx.dev`. If you never use Relay mode or a Ferryx account, none of it exists for you. Where the code has no expiry, the retention is listed as "kept until account removal": nothing deletes it until an operator removes it on request.
 
-- **Machine ownership:** The relay binds each machine ID to the Ed25519 public key that first enrolled it, and writes that map to `machine_keys.json` (`src-tauri/src/remote/relay_server.rs:909`). The default path is `~/.ferryx/relay/machine_keys.json`, or `FERRYX_RELAY_DATA_DIR`/`FERRYX_RELAY_KEY_FILE` when set (`:518-531`). The account service also records each enrolled machine (machine ID, display name, platform, public keys, enrollment and last-seen times) in its `machines` table (`src-tauri/src/account/store_sqlite/schema.rs:133-145`). Retention: kept until account removal.
-- **Billing state:** Account and billing records live in the SQLite store `account-store.sqlite3` (`STORE_SQLITE_FILENAME`, `src-tauri/src/remote/relay_server.rs:9887`, `src-tauri/src/account/store_sqlite/mod.rs:10`). Billing tables hold the plan, seats, host packs, status, end date, the Lemon Squeezy customer ID and portal URL (`subscriptions`), the grace and stop timestamps (`billing_states`), and a SHA-256 hash, name, and outcome for each received webhook (`payment_events`) (`src-tauri/src/account/store_sqlite/schema.rs:172-203`). Retention: kept until account removal; `payment_events` rows contain no account identifier and have no expiry.
-- **Peer IP addresses:** The relay reads the connecting TCP peer address (`peer_ip`, `src-tauri/src/remote/relay_server.rs:3798`, defined at `:3518`) to rate-limit connection and pairing attempts. These counters are kept in memory per IP (`:467-468`) and dropped after a 60-second window or lockout ends (`:489`, `:917-923`). The relay code does not write peer IPs to disk or to its own log lines; the hosting provider or a reverse proxy in front of the relay can keep its own access logs. Separately, the account service stores the requester IP taken from `cf-connecting-ip` or `x-forwarded-for` on each pending machine request (`src-tauri/src/account/machine_requests.rs:114-125,275`). Retention: the request's 15-minute lifetime plus 7 days (`src-tauri/src/account/machine_requests.rs:22`, `src-tauri/src/account/store.rs:19,356-358`).
-- **Email address and code hashes:** Signing in stores your email address in the `users` table (`src-tauri/src/account/store_sqlite/schema.rs:101-105`) in the account data directory (`docs/account-service.md:29`). Login codes, pairing capabilities, and session bearers are stored only as hashes (`docs/account-service.md:63-64`). Retention: the email address is kept until account removal. Sessions expire after 30 days and login codes after 10 minutes (`src-tauri/src/account/store.rs:13-14`). Expired sessions are purged on the next store write (`:359`); a login code row is removed when the app collects its session or when an expired code is presented (`src-tauri/src/account/service.rs:865,877`). Login emails go out through Resend when the operator configures `RESEND_API_KEY` (`src-tauri/src/account/mailer.rs:429-435`), so Resend receives the address and the message.
-- **Payment processor:** Paid plans are sold through Lemon Squeezy, which handles checkout, quantity changes, and webhooks (`docs/account-service.md:111-114`). Checkout sends Lemon Squeezy your account ID and, when known, your email address (`src-tauri/src/account/billing/lemonsqueezy.rs:1279-1288`). Card and invoice data stay with Lemon Squeezy and never reach the Ferryx account service. Retention: Ferryx keeps only the `subscriptions` fields listed above, until account removal; Lemon Squeezy keeps its records under its own policy.
